	abstract = {The rapid growth of multimedia data introduces an increasing demand for sufficient safeguards to uphold confidentiality, authenticity, and integrity (i.e., response to emerging threats). Depending on their scalability, trustworthiness, and post-quantum security, the reliance on isolated classic crypto protocols and centralized authentication mechanisms, may be drastically reduced. In this paper, we will explore a set of requirements regarding Integrated Quantum-Road Multimedia Security (IQMS) solutions employing both the quantum-resilience properties of Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) and Quantum Key Distribution (QKD), along with blockchain-based integrity verification/principles and lightweight chaos-hybrid cryptography. This work provides varying levels of significance. First, decentralized authentication approaches reduce the potential risk exposure (e.g., tampering, pirating, and unauthorized use) while providing improved security due to the reliance on multi-layered verification - blockchain and chaos-based hybrid cryptography. Moreover, PQC and QKD efforts provide some measure of security from theoretical quantum computer attacks using the Shor and Grover Algorithms against classical and existing weaknesses in cryptography. The performance tests also confirmed that IQMS exceeded hybrid AES+ECC and classical AES/RSA classes. The framework had an amazing accuracy of > 96.8% and a classification percent of 95.2 compared to the baseline model (97). Additionally, the accuracy was achieved without affecting latency-light that would make PDR perhaps meaningless for real-time use; likewise, the proposed IQMS had a PDR of 98.4 with total energy consumption of 12.5 J/transaction (that's less than a quarter of ECC-based techniques). This evidence quantitatively establishes how IQMS can conceptually serve as a basis for science developing scalable, efficient, sustainable, and quantum-ready level of security for next-generation multimedia ecosystems. As mentioned, IQMS is more than a solution to advance security applications for multimedia - it aims to first continue to develop robust frameworks that furnish efforts to address dilemmas in the classical and quantum epochs. Β© This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License. License details: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/},
