	abstract = {A new era in the security of communication channels in Biomedical Data Ecosystems has begun with the advent of quantum-based privacy-preserving technologies such as Quantum Key Distribution (QKD). Quantum assaults can compromise hashing functions and public-key cryptosystems, putting genomic data at danger. The research introduces Q-GenCrytoProtect, a quantum-resistant cryptographic architecture for genomic privacy in decentralized biomedical data ecosystems. The proposed system uses lattice-based post-quantum signatures, multi-key homomorphic encryption, and a new quantum-resilient hash function for high-dimensional genomic data integrity. Q-GenProtect uses blockchain technology for decentralized key management, dynamic and immutable access controls, and reliable audit trails to protect against impending quantum risks. The approach supports large-scale genomic repositories, safe multiparty genomic computation without data exposure, and easy integration with decentralized infrastructures. The extensive research and practical tests that show Q-GenProtect is quantum-resistant, scalable, and computationally efficient have raised genomic privacy and governance standards. This innovation ensures quantum computing-era biological data communication. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
