	affiliations = {B.S. Abdur Rahman Crescent Institute of Science and Technology, Department of Computer Applications, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {Conventional cryptosystems that make use of number-theoretic RSA and ECC are facing the most significant threat thanks to the emergence of quantum computing technologies. People are searching for reliable digital signatures that are compatible with post-quantum systems with a great deal of urgency because it appears that these systems are on the verge of becoming extinct. An new blockchain model that makes use of overhead-aware post-quantum cryptography optimization is presented as a result of this research. In addition to providing audit trails and key management, the blockchain layer also provides decentralized and tamper-proof validation operations. At the same time, optimization strategies that make computations, key sizes, and communications less complicated improve the performance of the system. Due to the fact that it is both scalable and energy-efficient, the model that has been described here is ideal for Internet of Things and edge networks. The results of the experiments demonstrate that it is possible to reduce latency and resource utilization without making the level of cryptographic security less secure. Through the use of this technology, the foundation is laid for the construction of secure digital communication networks in the future. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
